id: E2168
error_signature: upstream stress-style validate program with compile-time iteration constant (ITERATE/LOOP define) runs for hours on shared OHOS device, OOM-killed or never finishes inside make check
match_keywords: ITERATE,compile-time constant,stress test,make check timeout,OOM killed,shared device,thread oversubscription,CORES,barrier,epoch,regressions,test window,iteration override,partial execution
category: testing,strategy,concurrency
severity: medium
root_cause: Concurrency libraries ship stress-style validate programs whose iteration counts are compile-time constants (ifndef-guarded defines such as ITERATE 5000000). configure probes CORES from /proc/cpuinfo (20) while the container/cgroup exposes fewer cores (8), so the test runs oversubscribed on a shared multi-tenant device — a single module takes hours of CPU, may be OOM-killed, and blocks the whole make check.
rec_approach: Before scheduling the test window, read the test sources for ITERATE/thread constants and the progress output format. Prefer compile-time override (pass the original CFLAGS plus one extra -DITERATE=N to make) over editing test sources; keep thread counts, argv and per-iteration correctness assertions identical to upstream. Declare every overridden program item-by-item in the PR upstream-test-modification section (file, reason, change, result). On shared devices run at low priority (nice 19) and gate with device health probes (MemFree plus fork probe).
solution_cmds: |
  # 1. read the constants before estimating the window
  grep -n "define ITERATE\|CORES" regressions/*/validate/*.c
  # 2. override at compile time only (original CFLAGS + one extra -D), do NOT edit sources
  make clean
  make barrier_centralized CFLAGS="$ORIG_CFLAGS -DITERATE=500000"
  nice -n 19 ./barrier_centralized 20 1 1   # keep upstream argv and thread count
verification: Each reduced-iteration program still executes the full per-iteration correctness assertions and exits 0; module RC and per-program logs match the declared counts. PR records the original constant, the override value and the evidence (original-run hours and OOM log) next to the modification table.
fallback: If a 1/10 iteration run still cannot finish, report partial execution honestly (N_executed over N_static with reasons and logs, PARTIAL basis) instead of claiming a full pass; never delete the failing test or silently shrink the denominator.
doc_refs: E429
applies_to: ck,liburcu,xthread,any-concurrency-library-stress-tests
last_updated: 2026-09-12
